OL,3,AHow India became dangerously addicted
OL,4,Ato Chinese imports
OL,5,
OL,6,FRetailers were up in arms and said that
OL,7,Fdomestic firms could never match the
OL,8,Fforeign-made stuff. But the combination
OL,9,Fof higher customs duties and quality
OL,10,Fcontrol standards worked.
OL,12,FIndian imports of toys fell by a third
OL,13,Ffrom nearly $300m (#227m) in 2020 to
OL,14,F$100m this year, while exports rose
OL,15,Ffrom around $129m to $200m in the same
OL,16,Fperiod. Moreover, the country was able
OL,17,Fto drastically reduce its dependence on
OL,18,FChina, which held a 70% share of the
OL,19,Flocal toy market.
